    "verified_source_behavior": "Explicit descriptor tactics bypass per-forward algorithm-list enumeration, reuse CPU descriptor buffers and memoize native validation; default-1 path remains unchanged."
  },
  "observations": [
    "Normal public ordinal0 took about 204\u2013206us per eager call; seeding only the already-enumerated algorithm list reduced this to about 71\u201376us across three workers. The median paired seeded/unseeded ratio was 0.345343, a 65.5% reduction for this diagnostic intervention.",
    "The corresponding default-1 intervention control increased by about 1.1% (median paired ratio 1.011412). Every public variant still constructed fresh runners and used actual cached-winner lookup.",
    "Repeated 100-result heuristic enumeration occurred for normal public ordinal0, returning 8 candidates. Seeded public ordinal0 and prepared retained ordinal0 performed no heuristic enumeration. Default paths retained their one-result query.",
    "All observed algorithm descriptors/configurations and GPU launch signatures matched across the variants for this case. The eager discrepancy therefore has material recurring CPU algorithm-list setup cost; this evidence does not require a better GPU algorithm selected by default.",
    "Prepared retained runners took about 10us eagerly while all graph timings were approximately 4us. Retention removes several public and lookup layers together and is not a single-component attribution.",
    "This is a common FlashInfer 0.7.2 execution-path issue affecting cached explicit tactics from either v1 or v2. No autotuner profiling ran; no v2-only regression or full-model speedup is established."
  ],
